  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "34674468",
      "title": "Adding Backend Code & Redirecting",
      "lectureOrder": 21,
      "videoOrder": 17,
      "sourceHash": "59ca793c40f08425ad6579bcca635859e74eaed2083d0f784c544f3d257f6338",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.04,
          "end": 4.44,
          "en": "Now what do we want to do here in action?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.44,
          "end": 7.29,
          "en": "Of course, we wanna get the data entered into this form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.29,
          "end": 11.37,
          "en": "and then store it as a new note in this notes.json file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.37,
          "end": 13.713,
          "en": "with help of these utility methods here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15,
          "end": 18.45,
          "en": "For that, we first of all need to extract the data submitted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.45,
          "end": 22.65,
          "en": "by that form and thankfully that super easy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.65,
          "end": 24.96,
          "en": "if you're using a form as we're doing it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.96,
          "end": 27,
          "en": "Then the browser out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27,
          "end": 29.61,
          "en": "of the box takes all the inputs that are",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.61,
          "end": 32.04,
          "en": "in the form and puts them into an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.04,
          "end": 34.92,
          "en": "which is attached to the outgoing post request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.92,
          "end": 36.87,
          "en": "The browser does this for you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.87,
          "end": 39.57,
          "en": "You don't have to do it manually.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.57,
          "end": 42.09,
          "en": "It will not be in js format, but some other format,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 42.09,
          "end": 43.68,
          "en": "but that does not matter here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.68,
          "end": 47.913,
          "en": "The outgoing post request will include all the input data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.87,
          "end": 51.75,
          "en": "Now you'll be able to extract the input data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 51.75,
          "end": 55.26,
          "en": "with help of these names that you assigned to your inputs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 55.26,
          "end": 58.98,
          "en": "and text areas and whatever you have in your forms.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.98,
          "end": 62.37,
          "en": "So you must have the name attribute on your inputs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.37,
          "end": 65.13,
          "en": "And then these name values are of course up to you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.13,
          "end": 69.96000000000001,
          "en": "here I chose title and content, so we don't have to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.96000000000001,
          "end": 73.38,
          "en": "extract any values in our client side React code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.38,
          "end": 77.01,
          "en": "We don't have to use two-way binding or refs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 77.01,
          "end": 78.45,
          "en": "We just submit a form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 78.45,
          "end": 80.973,
          "en": "and we have these names on our input elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 81.9,
          "end": 82.733,
          "en": "And then here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 82.733,
          "end": 87.18,
          "en": "in the action we actually get an object provided by Remix",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.18,
          "end": 90.69,
          "en": "because Remix is the thing calling this action function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 90.69,
          "end": 94.14,
          "en": "And Remix gives us a data object that includes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 94.14,
          "end": 95.943,
          "en": "various pieces of information.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 96.96000000000001,
          "end": 98.07,
          "en": "Most importantly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 98.07,
          "end": 102.93,
          "en": "this data object includes a request object with details",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 102.93,
          "end": 106.053,
          "en": "about the request that was submitted by the form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 106.97999999999999,
          "end": 109.97999999999999,
          "en": "And here I'll simply use object destructuring to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 109.97999999999999,
          "end": 113.223,
          "en": "directly get access to that request object like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 114.72,
          "end": 118.14,
          "en": "Now this request object has a form data method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 118.14,
          "end": 119.37299999999999,
          "en": "which we can execute.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 120.42,
          "end": 122.13,
          "en": "This actually returns a promise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 122.13,
          "end": 125.49,
          "en": "And to use async weight here, I'll add the async keyword",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 125.49,
          "end": 127.77,
          "en": "in front of this function, which is okay",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 127.77,
          "end": 130.2,
          "en": "this action function can be an async function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 130.2,
          "end": 131.82,
          "en": "or a non async function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 131.82,
          "end": 133.86,
          "en": "It does not matter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 133.86,
          "end": 137.793,
          "en": "And I'll then a await calling request form data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 138.87,
          "end": 141.84,
          "en": "The result is a form data object, which actually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 141.84,
          "end": 145.86,
          "en": "gives us access to the input values that were entered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 145.86,
          "end": 147.453,
          "en": "into these form inputs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 149.52,
          "end": 152.25,
          "en": "So that's how we can extract that submitted data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 152.25,
          "end": 154.47,
          "en": "from the incoming request.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 154.47,
          "end": 157.89,
          "en": "And we're embracing a lot of web standards here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 157.89,
          "end": 160.71,
          "en": "the standard request object that's constructed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 160.71,
          "end": 162.96,
          "en": "by the browser and sent to the backend",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 162.96,
          "end": 167.19,
          "en": "and the standard form behavior that's built into browsers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 167.19,
          "end": 170.22,
          "en": "We don't reinvent the wheel by riding our own logic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 170.22,
          "end": 172.44,
          "en": "Instead, we embrace these standards",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 172.44,
          "end": 175.05,
          "en": "and we get access to all this submitted data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 175.05,
          "end": 178.47,
          "en": "with one simple line of code here on the back end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 178.47,
          "end": 180.12,
          "en": "And keep in mind, this is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 180.12,
          "end": 183.33,
          "en": "on the backend here since it's in the action function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 183.33,
          "end": 184.95,
          "en": "Now that's the first step.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 184.95,
          "end": 189.27,
          "en": "As a next step, I'll add a note data object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 189.27,
          "end": 194.27,
          "en": "a brand new JavaScript object where I add a title property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 195.09,
          "end": 198.27,
          "en": "And then we can access this form data object here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 198.27,
          "end": 201.39,
          "en": "which we got by calling form data like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 201.39,
          "end": 204.36,
          "en": "And there we can call the special get method to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 204.36,
          "end": 205.74,
          "en": "extract our values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 205.74,
          "end": 209.01,
          "en": "by the name we assigned to the input elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 209.01,
          "end": 211.77,
          "en": "So here, since I used title",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 211.77,
          "end": 214.89,
          "en": "and content as names for my input elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 214.89,
          "end": 218.46,
          "en": "I can use title for extracting the title",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 218.46,
          "end": 221.46,
          "en": "and content for extracting the content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 221.46,
          "end": 224.85,
          "en": "And I store these extracted values in this object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 224.85,
          "end": 228.15,
          "en": "Alternatively, there is a shortcut you can use to build",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 228.15,
          "end": 232.47,
          "en": "in object, object with a capital O at the beginning",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 232.47,
          "end": 237.47,
          "en": "and call from entries and pass your form data object to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 238.14,
          "end": 241.35,
          "en": "This will basically convert this form data object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 241.35,
          "end": 242.82,
          "en": "which would require the use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 242.82,
          "end": 247.53,
          "en": "of methods to extract the data that's submitted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 247.53,
          "end": 250.503,
          "en": "into a standard plain JavaScript object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 251.43,
          "end": 255.42,
          "en": "And this JavaScript object will have a title",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 255.42,
          "end": 258.72,
          "en": "and a content property because those were the names attached",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 258.72,
          "end": 260.163,
          "en": "to the inputs in the form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 261.12,
          "end": 263.493,
          "en": "So that's how we get hold of the user input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 264.33,
          "end": 266.94,
          "en": "Now here we could add validation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 266.94,
          "end": 269.64,
          "en": "but we won't do so for the moment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 269.64,
          "end": 273.48,
          "en": "And instead, I now wanna add this note data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 273.48,
          "end": 276.6,
          "en": "as a new note to my existing notes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 276.6,
          "end": 278.94,
          "en": "To do that, I'll first of all get hold",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 278.94,
          "end": 281.25,
          "en": "of my existing notes that might be stored",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 281.25,
          "end": 283.77,
          "en": "in this notes.json files already",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 283.77,
          "end": 286.8,
          "en": "by calling get stored notes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 286.8,
          "end": 289.08,
          "en": "And this is a function that must be imported",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 289.08,
          "end": 293.28,
          "en": "from this data folder and then notes in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 293.28,
          "end": 296.52,
          "en": "So I'm using one of the two utility functions to find",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 296.52,
          "end": 299.433,
          "en": "in this data folder in the notes.json file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 300.6,
          "end": 303.51,
          "en": "Now get stored notes actually returns a promise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 303.51,
          "end": 306.393,
          "en": "So here I'll wait it like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 307.32,
          "end": 309.45,
          "en": "And with that I got my existing notes that might",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 309.45,
          "end": 311.01,
          "en": "have been stored before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 311.01,
          "end": 312.75,
          "en": "because I of course don't wanna lose them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 312.75,
          "end": 317.75,
          "en": "If I add a new one, then I take my note data object here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 318.54,
          "end": 322.56,
          "en": "and I add a brand new property to it an id property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 322.56,
          "end": 326.22,
          "en": "because I wanna have a unique identifier for every note.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 326.22,
          "end": 329.16,
          "en": "And here I'll simply use the current date converted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 329.16,
          "end": 332.04,
          "en": "to an ISOString as an id.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 332.04,
          "end": 333.63,
          "en": "Theoretically it's not unique",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 333.63,
          "end": 337.11,
          "en": "because two notes could be added at exactly the same moment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 337.11,
          "end": 338.86,
          "en": "but for this demo it's good enough.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 340.38,
          "end": 342.21,
          "en": "So with that, we now got the node data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 342.21,
          "end": 343.59000000000003,
          "en": "we got the existing notes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 343.59000000000003,
          "end": 346.86,
          "en": "Now we can create an updated notes object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 346.86,
          "end": 350.79,
          "en": "by using the existing notes and calling Concat on it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 350.79,
          "end": 354.123,
          "en": "and concatenating this note data with the new note.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 355.65,
          "end": 359.13,
          "en": "And then this updated notes object should be stored back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 359.13,
          "end": 360.633,
          "en": "into notes.json.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 361.47,
          "end": 362.303,
          "en": "And that can be done",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 362.303,
          "end": 365.808,
          "en": "with that second utility function, the store notes function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 365.808,
          "end": 370.32,
          "en": "which expects to receive the new notes that should be stored",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 370.32,
          "end": 373.65,
          "en": "and therefore here we now call store notes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 373.65,
          "end": 377.04,
          "en": "which is also imported from the data folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 377.04,
          "end": 378.67,
          "en": "From the notes js file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 380.76,
          "end": 384.033,
          "en": "and two store notes we pass our updated notes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 385.83,
          "end": 388.11,
          "en": "Now this, all the returns are promise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 388.11,
          "end": 390.06,
          "en": "and I will await this promise because now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 390.06,
          "end": 393.48,
          "en": "there's one last thing we have to do in this action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 393.48,
          "end": 395.67,
          "en": "And what would that be?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 395.67,
          "end": 397.86,
          "en": "Well, assuming that that all works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 397.86,
          "end": 401.85,
          "en": "we dare after might want to redirect the user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 401.85,
          "end": 405.09000000000003,
          "en": "Actually for this page, we don't need to redirect the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 405.09000000000003,
          "end": 406.44,
          "en": "because we'll render a list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 406.44,
          "end": 410.1,
          "en": "of notes right below this form here in the future.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 410.1,
          "end": 412.74,
          "en": "But on other pages you might have a separate page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 412.74,
          "end": 416.15999999999997,
